us' and an empty lesson_url (whitespace-only behaves identically per the source's trim), video_url '', and the existing fixture's other fields (video_title 'Test Video Title', snippet 'Test snippet text', 10s-20s)","id":"AC-3","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation, exercised by app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts (vitest)","then":"the returned string starts with '- ', contains no '](', and still contains its > \"snippet\" blockquote — concretely, '> \"Test snippet text\"' for the existing fixture","when":"formatCitation(citation) is called"},{"given":"a default/'youtube' citation whose video_url parses but has no 'v' query parameter (existing fixture 'https://www.youtube.com/') and a non-blank snippet ('Test snippet text' in the existing fixture) — the second YouTube fallback trigger named in the issue background","id":"AC-4","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation, exercised by app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts (vitest)","then":"the returned string starts with '- ', contains the snippet blockquote on its own line ('> \"Test snippet text\"'), still contains '(timestamp link unavailable)' and '0:10–0:20', and contains no '[Test Video Title](' link syntax","when":"formatCitation(citation) is called"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["Every currently-green assertion in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keeps passing: the YouTube fallback outputs keep containing the video title, '(timestamp link unavailable)' and '0:10–0:20' and keep NOT containing '[Test Video Title](' link syntax; the Dynamous no-lesson_url output keeps containing the title, the range and the snippet blockquote while containing no ']('.","The console.warn behavior is preserved on both YouTube fallback triggers (new URL() throwing, and URL parsed but missing the v parameter): the message stays exactly '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"<video_url>\"' and neither existing warn call site is dropped, whether they are kept separate or consolidated behind one shared fallback return.","formatCitation's early return is unchanged: blank, whitespace-only or missing snippet still yields '' (empty string) before any URL handling.","The two valid link paths produce output identical to today: YouTube with a parsed v parameter returns '- [<title>](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<v>&t=<start>s) — <range>' followed by a newline and a two-space-indented blockquote line '> \"<snippet>\"'; Dynamous with a non-empty lesson_url returns '- [<title>](<lesson_url>) — <range>' followed by the same newline + blockquote line.","formatSources keeps its current contract: '**Sources:**' header, per-citation outputs joined with a newline, no list markers added by formatSources itself (the '- ' marker is formatCitation's responsibility), and the empty/null/undefined guards unchanged; exportConversationAsMarkdown's header, role mapping, filename slug and saveAs call are unchanged.","Fallback citation entries are plain-text list items, never markdown links: no '[<title>](' or '](' substring may appear in any fallback output (YouTube unparsable, YouTube no-v, Dynamous without lesson_url).","The snippet blockquote on fixed fallback paths begins its own line and matches the blockquote line shape the two link paths already emit (newline, then a two-space-indented '> \"<snippet>\"'), so fallback and link citations render identically as markdown list items.","Only app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts changes among production files; the only other changed file is app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts (acceptance cases added there). No changes to CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, src/lib/api.ts, the backend, schema, deploy/, .github/ or any .env file.","No new or version-changed packages in either ecosystem — the fix is pure string formatting and the tests use the existing vitest setup (with the file-saver mock already present in the test file); this contract's dependencies array is empty.","Existing cases in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts are neither modified nor deleted (only new acceptance cases are added); their labels may go slightly stale (e.g. 'title-only' describing the old fallback) but their assertions must all keep passing unchanged.","Frontend gates stay green with the change: bun run tsc --noEmit, bun x biome check src, and the full vitest suite (bun run test) from app/frontend/."],"issue":{"number":49,"title":"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed"},"out_of_scope":["Backend, database schema, Alembic migrations, and any dependency changes (no new or upgraded packages in either ecosystem).","app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, any other component/hook/page, and the Citation type in app/frontend/src/lib/api.ts.","The valid-URL YouTube path and the valid-lesson_url Dynamous path — their output strings must not change (issue: 'Out of scope').","formatTimestamp behavior, the export header, and the filename slug logic.","Markdown-escaping or sanitising snippet content — snippets continue to be interpolated verbatim on every path, as today; adding escaping would change all paths and is a separate concern.","Deploy configs, Dockerfiles, systemd units, .env files, and the factory trust root (factory_kernel/, .factory/, harness/, scripts/factory_*, tests/factory/)."],"risks":["Both YouTube fallback return sites exhibit the bug (the new URL() catch branch and the parses-but-no-v branch); a fix touching only the catch branch would leave the no-v path still dropping the snippet — AC-4 exists to guard exactly this.","The existing test pins the exact console.warn message ('[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"not-a-url\"'); consolidating the two warn call sites during the fix must not alter the message text or drop either emission.","The red loop is deferred (repro record mode 'deferred'): the AC-1..AC-4 acceptance cases must be authored in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts and proven RED on the unchanged tree first — AC-1 failing around the literal '> \"Relevant text\"' — then GREEN after the fix; landing the fix before proving red forfeits the regression guarantee.","Blast radius is small and verified: only ChatArea.tsx imports this module (exportConversationAsMarkdown); no other frontend file consumes formatCitation/formatSources — but the kernel's full vitest run remains the backstop for any unseen consumer.","The snippet is interpolated verbatim into the blockquote today (no markdown escaping); the fix must preserve that interpolation as-is on fallback paths rather than 'improving' it, since escaping would change every citation path and is out of scope for this issue."],"summary":"Fix the three fallback return sites of formatCitation in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts so every emitted citation entry keeps the leading '- ' list marker and the transcript-snippet blockquote: the YouTube fallbacks (video_url unparsable, or parsed but without a v parameter) must include the '> \"<snippet>\"' blockquote and the '- ' marker while retaining the title, '(timestamp link unavailable)', the timestamp range and both existing console.warn calls; the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback gains the '- ' marker while keeping its existing snippet blockquote. Acceptance tests for AC-1..AC-4 are added to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts (proven RED on the unchanged tree before the fix, per the repro record) and every existing case there keeps passing. Valid link paths, formatTimestamp, the export header and the filename slug are untouched; no new dependencies.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"4e9263bfd8ff30be86e272c7527f41897660bc68bcdbb3603f5e378a2bd11419","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"],"AC-4":["app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"10caeb48a07432dc9d3004434549e61daf4684f7a6136c55e109cdd56bc31956","contract_sha256":"4e9263bfd8ff30be86e272c7527f41897660bc68bcdbb3603f5e378a2bd11419","data_flows":["Citation (default/'youtube', video_url parses with a v param) -> formatCitation -> unchanged '- [<title>](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<v>&t=<start>s) — <range>' + newline + two-space-indented '> \"<snippet>\"'","Citation (default/'youtube', video_url unparsable OR parses without a v param) -> formatCitation -> console.warn (existing message) + '- <title> (timestamp link unavailable) — <range>' + newline + two-space-indented '> \"<snippet>\"'","Citation (source_type 'dynamous', empty/whitespace lesson_url) -> formatCitation -> '- <title> — <range>' + newline + two-space-indented '> \"<snippet>\"'","Citation with blank/whitespace/missing snippet -> formatCitation -> '' (early return, unchanged)","Citation[] -> formatSources -> '\\n\\n**Sources:**\\n' + formatCitation outputs joined with '\\n' (unchanged; the '- ' marker remains formatCitation's responsibility)"],"invariants":["Every currently-green assertion in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keeps passing unchanged; existing cases are neither modified nor deleted — only new acceptance cases are added inside the existing describe('formatCitation') block.","The console.warn on both YouTube fallback triggers keeps the exact message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"<video_url>\"' and neither trigger loses its emission; the fix keeps the two existing call sites separate.","formatCitation's early return is unchanged: blank, whitespace-only or missing snippet yields '' before any URL handling.","The two valid link paths (YouTube with a parsed v param; Dynamous with a non-empty lesson_url) produce output byte-identical to today: '- [<titl